    "created_at": "2022-03-29T08:36:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-29T08:36:27Z",
    "body": "One of the design principles we tried to follow was \"users shouldn't be punished for race conditions outside of their control\". We appear to have failed in this case.\r\n\r\nI don't have a good sense for whether it would be safe to change this behaviour. Could there be a non-trivial number of scripts depending on it?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
